Locally authored vz executable permission preflight correction for pinned youki 0.7.0.
Apply AFTER seccomp-exec.patch, tenant-root.patch and runtime-log.patch.
Not an upstream-reviewed backport. Runtime change is only 0001 -> 0111.

Rationale: vz privately stages Docker binaries at mode 0700; Moby's --init binds
that same docker-init inode to /sbin/docker-init. Upstream's other-execute-only
preflight rejects it despite valid owner/root execution. Retain regular-file
validation and permit any execute bit. The existing execvp syscall continues
to enforce actual credentials, DAC, ACLs, and mount execution policy. No artifact
mode, ownership, credential, namespace, seccomp, or init configuration changes.

--- a/crates/libcontainer/src/workload/default.rs
+++ b/crates/libcontainer/src/workload/default.rs
@@ -130,21 +130,267 @@
     use std::os::unix::fs::PermissionsExt;
     let metadata = path.metadata()?;
     let permissions = metadata.permissions();
-    // we have to check if the path is file and the execute bit
-    // is set. In case of directories, the execute bit is also set,
-    // so have to check if this is a file or not
-    Ok(metadata.is_file() && permissions.mode() & 0o001 != 0)
+    // This is a structural preflight, not an authorization decision. Requiring
+    // other-execute rejects valid owner/group-only executables, such as a
+    // private 0700 docker-init bind mount. Keep the regular-file requirement
+    // and accept any execute bit; the unchanged execvp call lets the kernel
+    // enforce actual credentials, DAC, ACLs and mount execution policy.
+    Ok(metadata.is_file() && permissions.mode() & 0o111 != 0)
 }
 
